(5647874, 819675, 52549, '<td valign="top">Great image. Different and interesting.</td>', 'Great image. Different and interesting.', '2009-09-15 11:57:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(5647974, 819247, 66494, '<td valign="top">Beautiful Sandy. Just clicked on the challenge results and immediately recognized this beautiful falls in Oregon. I hope you visited Crater Lake too while you were there.</td>', 'Beautiful Sandy. Just clicked on the challenge results and immediately recognized this beautiful falls in Oregon. I hope you visited Crater Lake too while you were there.', '2009-09-15 13:26:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(5648509, 819688, 49773, '<td valign="top">Pretty good.</td>', 'Pretty good.', '2009-09-15 18:55:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(5648610, 819608, 87808, '<td valign="top">Okay seriously, I am getting one of your shots again!!!!!  I am sure you are sick of my ''indepth'' comments by now LOL<br/> <br/>Anywayssssssssssss,,,,, In voting I gave this an 8, here are the reasons why. <br/> <br/>I didn''t think that this was over exposed, I think this could have been dodged a little more to bring out those tiles.  now i know that you horizon is not tilted, but the under neigh of the bridge is and that is more prominent because it is red.<br/> <br/>so a little more expose would work with this shot, you are sharp and clean on your lines. saturations are good<br/> <br/>I still think this shot is great<br/> <br/></td>', 'Okay seriously, I am getting one of your shots again!!!!!  I am sure you are sick of my ''indepth'' comments by now LOL Anywayssssssssssss,,,,, In voting I gave this an 8, here are the reasons why.  I didn''t think that this was over exposed, I think this could have been dodged a little more to bring out those tiles.  now i know that you horizon is not tilted, but the under neigh of the bridge is and that is more prominent because it is red. so a little more expose would work with this shot, you are sharp and clean on your lines. saturations are good I still think this shot is great ', '2009-09-15 21:10:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(5648652, 819702, 79720, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by IreneM:</b></div><hr/><i> I was a bit off in my "top 3" prediction but still glad you made top 10. Congrats, David. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>That''s OK, Irene...I still luvs ya anyway. ;-)</td>', 'Originally posted by IreneM: I was a bit off in my "top 3" prediction but still glad you made top 10. Congrats, David.  That''s OK, Irene...I still luvs ya anyway. ;-)', '2009-09-15 21:43:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(5649518, 819541, 39850, '<td valign="top"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/35000-39999/39850/800/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_809051.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/35000-39999/39850/800/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_809051.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/35000-39999/39850/800/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_809051.jpg"/> <br/> <br/><u>Critique Club Critique</u> <br/> <br/><b>First Impressions</b> <br/>Good for a Where''s Waldo Challenge.  Maybe not even subtle enough.  I didn''t vote in this Challenge.<br/> <br/><b>Photograph Information, Technicals &amp; Composition Review</b> <br/>I like your composition, the lighting and scene are pleasant and warm.<br/> <br/>The HDR use is new to me, especially in regard to using it in Challenge entries.  I find that with this image, the HDR has enhanced the nice warm lighting, which is good, but what bothers me is the few ''whiteish marks'' around the boy''s lower torso.  I can''t discern what they are and can''t help but wonder if they are a result of overlays from different frames.  Apologies in advance if wrong.<br/> <br/>There is some slight blur (again, could be movement), however it grows on me the more I look at it and it adds to the overall softness of the image.<br/> <br/>Lastly, 720 in this Challenge would have strengthened your entry (the ''hidden person'' aspect aside), if the quality was there.<br/> <br/><b>Comments, Score &amp; Placement Review</b> <br/>27/73 is a good placement and your score of 5.66 doesn''t really reflect that.  I can only surmise that it is because there were a low number of entries in this Challenge and it was an overall low scoring Challenge.<br/> <br/>Most of your commenters like your coloring and the light, however there isn''t too much feedback on why you received an average score of 6.5 from them.<br/> <br/><b>Summary</b> <br/>A little more subtle with the person for this Challenge and possibly a little more context/foreground, with the technicals slightly more refined (even if leaving it soft, but the HDR/movement issues eliminated), would have made this a stronger entry in my opinion.</td>', '  Critique Club Critique  First Impressions Good for a Where''s Waldo Challenge.  Maybe not even subtle enough.  I didn''t vote in this Challenge. Photograph Information, Technicals & Composition Review I like your composition, the lighting and scene are pleasant and warm. The HDR use is new to me, especially in regard to using it in Challenge entries.  I find that with this image, the HDR has enhanced the nice warm lighting, which is good, but what bothers me is the few ''whiteish marks'' around the boy''s lower torso.  I can''t discern what they are and can''t help but wonder if they are a result of overlays from different frames.  Apologies in advance if wrong. There is some slight blur (again, could be movement), however it grows on me the more I look at it and it adds to the overall softness of the image. Lastly, 720 in this Challenge would have strengthened your entry (the ''hidden person'' aspect aside), if the quality was there. Comments, Score & Placement Review 27/73 is a good placement and your score of 5.66 doesn''t really reflect that.  I can only surmise that it is because there were a low number of entries in this Challenge and it was an overall low scoring Challenge. Most of your commenters like your coloring and the light, however there isn''t too much feedback on why you received an average score of 6.5 from them. Summary A little more subtle with the person for this Challenge and possibly a little more context/foreground, with the technicals slightly more refined (even if leaving it soft, but the HDR/movement issues eliminated), would have made this a stronger entry in my opinion.', '2009-09-16 08:35:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(5649545, 819145, 83395, '<td valign="top">Cool!  Nice $25 ribbon!  : )  It looks a little like your son is using a squatty.  : )</td>', 'Cool!  Nice $25 ribbon!  : )  It looks a little like your son is using a squatty.  : )', '2009-09-16 09:06:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(5649643, 819546, 42198, '<td valign="top">Yo Iain. I''m really happy for you, imma let you finish. But banmorn had one of the best photos of all time. Of all time.<br/> <br/>;-) j/k</td>', 'Yo Iain. I''m really happy for you, imma let you finish. But banmorn had one of the best photos of all time. Of all time. ;-) j/k', '2009-09-16 10:00:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(5650252, 819629, 52472, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club :)<br/> <br/>My first impression was a big WOW about the fantastic perspective!<br/> <br/>A key to great landscape photography is to recreate a 3D feeling with only 2 dimensions. You succeeded so perfectly that this image could be used as a textbook example. The sign does most of the job and I certainly do not agree with the comment which asks for leaving it out. There are loads of prominent lines in your composition, which are very interesting for the eye to be followed. They are nicely balanced by the curve of the bridge.<br/> <br/>The early time of the day gives a nice warm lighting with pleasant colors. The side lighting enhances the shape of the rocks. The focus and exposure seem perfect. But you should know that using small apertures creates diffraction blur, I''m not sure if you really needed that small for a good depth of field. So far so good for the technicals. But I am not convinced by your choice of HDR. One of the disadvantage of this technique is that it can produce quite flat color tones. If you look at the cliff for instance, there''s a terrible lack of detail (I thought it was from sharpening first). Also the rocks in the foreground could look better by increasing a bit the contrast in the mid-tones. Moreover, I cannot see any advantage you get from HDR in this specific case. If you just had some exposure issues in some areas, it could be more effective to work with layer masks.<br/> <br/>The subject (Waldo) is very difficult to make out. There''s a strangely colored ''rock'' between the utmost left pillars of the bridge which must be him. I know that the challenge is that he is difficult to be found, but once I do find him I want to distinguish a bit more.<br/> <br/>From my two last points you should have a possible explanation why your picture scored relatively low. And low it is for such an outstanding composition. As the composition is the hardest thing to learn in my opinion, I am pretty convinced that we will see some ribbons from you in a near future :)<br/> <br/>If you have any questions or remarks about this critique, feel free to contact me.<br/>Mike<br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club :) My first impression was a big WOW about the fantastic perspective! A key to great landscape photography is to recreate a 3D feeling with only 2 dimensions. You succeeded so perfectly that this image could be used as a textbook example. The sign does most of the job and I certainly do not agree with the comment which asks for leaving it out. There are loads of prominent lines in your composition, which are very interesting for the eye to be followed. They are nicely balanced by the curve of the bridge. The early time of the day gives a nice warm lighting with pleasant colors. The side lighting enhances the shape of the rocks. The focus and exposure seem perfect. But you should know that using small apertures creates diffraction blur, I''m not sure if you really needed that small for a good depth of field. So far so good for the technicals. But I am not convinced by your choice of HDR. One of the disadvantage of this technique is that it can produce quite flat color tones. If you look at the cliff for instance, there''s a terrible lack of detail (I thought it was from sharpening first). Also the rocks in the foreground could look better by increasing a bit the contrast in the mid-tones. Moreover, I cannot see any advantage you get from HDR in this specific case. If you just had some exposure issues in some areas, it could be more effective to work with layer masks. The subject (Waldo) is very difficult to make out. There''s a strangely colored ''rock'' between the utmost left pillars of the bridge which must be him. I know that the challenge is that he is difficult to be found, but once I do find him I want to distinguish a bit more. From my two last points you should have a possible explanation why your picture scored relatively low. And low it is for such an outstanding composition. As the composition is the hardest thing to learn in my opinion, I am pretty convinced that we will see some ribbons from you in a near future :) If you have any questions or remarks about this critique, feel free to contact me.Mike', '2009-09-16 17:50:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(5650330, 819145, 84668, '<td valign="top">I''d like some details of the editing process for this photo... Could you please post it?</td>', 'I''d like some details of the editing process for this photo... Could you please post it?', '2009-09-16 19:17:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(5650614, 819145, 96572, '<td valign="top">Excellent photo! Good job! The use of your son in this picture is perfect! Clever idea!</td>', 'Excellent photo! Good job! The use of your son in this picture is perfect! Clever idea!', '2009-09-16 22:33:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(5650619, 819713, 96572, '<td valign="top">Ok, this picture has been on the front page just for couple days but it just keep drawing me, over and over! I love this shot... I like how the thumbnail picture looks also!  What a creative picture! Congrats!</td>', 'Ok, this picture has been on the front page just for couple days but it just keep drawing me, over and over! I love this shot... I like how the thumbnail picture looks also!  What a creative picture! Congrats!', '2009-09-16 22:35:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(5650669, 819455, 87808, '<td valign="top">HI from the C Club<br/> <br/>You asked for a comment by one of the members of the critique Club<br/> <br/>I like your shot, it is very bright and breezy!<br/> <br/>I think that the only thing that hurt you a little here was it was so easy to find the Waldo!<br/> <br/>Everything else is just lovely, sharp, clean amazing reflections.<br/> <br/>You did a great job on this shot!</td>', 'HI from the C Club You asked for a comment by one of the members of the critique Club I like your shot, it is very bright and breezy! I think that the only thing that hurt you a little here was it was so easy to find the Waldo! Everything else is just lovely, sharp, clean amazing reflections. You did a great job on this shot!', '2009-09-16 22:54:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(5650676, 819619, 87808, '<td valign="top">HI from the C Club<br/> <br/>You asked for a comment by one of the members of the critique Club<br/> <br/>When I went through this challenge, I really liked this shot, but I have to admit i searched and searched and couldn''t find it.  After reading the comments, I can not believe I didn''t see it!!<br/> <br/>This is a fantastic shot, sharp, clean and on point.  There is not a lot you could have done with this shot as it really is just great. <br/> <br/>You have an amazing perspective and followed through with it!<br/> <br/>Well done</td>', 'HI from the C Club You asked for a comment by one of the members of the critique Club When I went through this challenge, I really liked this shot, but I have to admit i searched and searched and couldn''t find it.  After reading the comments, I can not believe I didn''t see it!! This is a fantastic shot, sharp, clean and on point.  There is not a lot you could have done with this shot as it really is just great.  You have an amazing perspective and followed through with it! Well done', '2009-09-16 22:58:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(5650686, 819474, 87808, '<td valign="top">HI from the C Club<br/> <br/>You asked for a comment by one of the members of the critique Club<br/> <br/>I gave this a 9 in voting, I think this was a brilliant idea and you executed it perfectly.  Waldo is there but you have to look, but he is not so obscure that you are searching for ever.<br/> <br/>Your POV and DOF is very good, your colours spot on, sharpness is excellent. <br/> <br/>Your score reflects how good this shot is</td>', 'HI from the C Club You asked for a comment by one of the members of the critique Club I gave this a 9 in voting, I think this was a brilliant idea and you executed it perfectly.  Waldo is there but you have to look, but he is not so obscure that you are searching for ever. Your POV and DOF is very good, your colours spot on, sharpness is excellent.  Your score reflects how good this shot is', '2009-09-16 23:01:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(5651285, 819145, 84668, '<td valign="top">Thanks, greatly appreciated! I don''t use to use Photoshop, even having it available here... I''ll try the actions and see how they come... But still I find that I can get same results on PSP X2, I really enjoy it much more than Photoshop.</td>', 'Thanks, greatly appreciated! I don''t use to use Photoshop, even having it available here... I''ll try the actions and see how they come... But still I find that I can get same results on PSP X2, I really enjoy it much more than Photoshop.', '2009-09-17 11:33:53.000000', NULL, 0),
