(5875422, 819673, 30861, '<td valign="top">Just saw this for the first time. Really an excellent piece of work. FWIW, "combining 4 different exposures to even out the light" is exactly what HDR actually is :-) The levels and masking you had to apply afterward is the manual equivalent of HDR tone mapping functions. What you did here represents the *origins* of HDR processing, which has now been automated by a lot of different programs. But there are MANY serious landscape photographers who still prefer to do it the way you did this, because it looks more natural that way.<br/> <br/>Obviously, I''m not one of ''em :-) But I admire this. Good work!</td>', 'Just saw this for the first time. Really an excellent piece of work. FWIW, "combining 4 different exposures to even out the light" is exactly what HDR actually is :-) The levels and masking you had to apply afterward is the manual equivalent of HDR tone mapping functions. What you did here represents the *origins* of HDR processing, which has now been automated by a lot of different programs. But there are MANY serious landscape photographers who still prefer to do it the way you did this, because it looks more natural that way. Obviously, I''m not one of ''em :-) But I admire this. Good work!', '2010-02-21 20:19:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(6039781, 819546, 118146, '<td valign="top">I love this picture! It''s the urban jungle :) Nice work!</td>', 'I love this picture! It''s the urban jungle :) Nice work!', '2010-06-03 20:49:04.000000', NULL, 0),
